 "notes": "The eleven horizontal lines are APPLIED polished-stainless inlay strips, not milled grooves - they read brighter than the face around them (1.1x at the lit top, 1.4x at the shaded foot), the opposite of a groove, and each is about 8 px tall. Their spacing is deliberately graduated and symmetric about mid height: gaps of 0.055, 0.080, 0.079, 0.107, 0.143, 0.141, 0.104, 0.080, 0.079, 0.055 of leaf height. Near jamb is the LEFT one - the camera sits right of the axis so the left reveal opens to 26 px while the right is a 3 px line. The handle is a bowed tube: its ends sit at x 0.17 and its belly reaches x 0.31."
